  "result": "I found the cause and wrote a plan for a one-line fix. Nothing has been changed yet because plan mode is on. I couldn't bring up the plan-approval prompt because that tool isn't available here, so I'm asking you directly instead.\n\n**Cause:** In `src/click/core.py:392`, a subcommand's context inherits the parent's whole `default_map` instead of the entry for its own name. With `default_map={\"sub\": {\"opt\": \"x\"}}`, the subcommand `sub` looks for `\"opt\"` at the top level, doesn't find it, and falls back to the option's normal default.\n\n**Fix:** Change that line to:\n```python\ndefault_map = parent.default_map.get(info_name)\n```\nThe surrounding check stays as it is. If a subcommand has no entry, it gets `None`, which is what happens today. This matches upstream Click.\n\n**Tests to add** in `tests/test_defaults.py`:\n- A subcommand picks up its entry from the parent's map.\n- Nested groups (`cli \u2192 grp \u2192 cmd`) resolve their own entries.\n- Keys set for the parent don't leak into a subcommand.\n- A `default_map` set directly on the subcommand still takes precedence.\n\n**To check it:** run `pytest tests/test_defaults.py tests/test_context.py tests/test_options.py -q`, then the full `pytest -q`.\n\nThe plan is saved at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\defaults-configured-through-default-map-mossy-leaf.md`. Should I go ahead and make the change?",
